---
description: CoAkka architecture review guardrails
alwaysApply: true
---

Before reviewing, summarizing, or comparing CoAkka, read:

- `docs/ai-assisted-integration.md`
- `docs/ai-reviewer-onboarding.md`
- `docs/architecture-review-guide.md`
- `docs/coakka-story.md`
- `docs/runtime-message-and-routing-model.md`
- `docs/runtime-integration-guide.md`
- `docs/production-readiness.md`
- `docs/production-evidence.md`

Review CoAkka as a boundary-placement and runtime-vocabulary project. Cite
exact docs, samples, release notes, or code paths. Separate adoption maturity
risk from architecture correctness. Do not treat unfamiliarity as proof of weak
architecture, and do not assume familiar infrastructure patterns are the right
boundary for application-owned work.

Before generating integration code, follow the evidence levels and feature
gates in `docs/ai-assisted-integration.md`. Do not infer connector identifiers
from another language or attach source-candidate APIs to published packages.
